{{also|kamel}}
==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|de|Kameel}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|kembel}}, {{m|gmh|kemmel}}, {{m|gmh|kamel}}, from Greek {{m|grc|κάμηλος}}, from a Semitic root.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|de|De-Kamel.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n||gen2=Kameles|Kamele}}

# a [[camel]]
# a dumb person

====Declension====
{{de-decl-noun-n|(e)s|e}}

====Hyponyms====
{{sense|camel}}
* {{l|de|[[einhöckerig]]es Kamel}}, {{l|de|[[einhöckrig]]es Kamel}}, {{l|de|Einhöcker}} = {{l|de|Dromedar}}
* {{l|de|[[zweihöckerig]]es Kamel}}, {{l|de|[[zweihöckrig]]es Kamel}}, {{l|de|Zweihöcker}} = {{l|de|Trampeltier}} (modern strict sense)

====Derived terms====
* {{l|de|Großkamel}} = {{l|de|Altweltkamel}}
* {{l|de|Kleinkamel}} = {{l|de|Neuweltkamel}}

